cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this model, please cite the software release."
title: "Multi-Commodity Maritime Chokepoint Transmission Model"
type: software
version: 0.5.0
date-released: 2026-08-12
authors:
  - family-names: Keen
    given-names: Jason
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An open-source scenario and Monte Carlo model for tracing immediate and
  lagged economic transmission from maritime chokepoint disruption through
  crude oil, LNG, fertilizer, and helium, with crude-grade segmentation and
  conditional ecological externalities.
keywords:
  - maritime chokepoints
  - geopolitical risk
  - energy markets
  - supply chains
  - Monte Carlo simulation
